; Number passages that all end the same way.
;
; A tester had documents made of passages of different lengths sharing an
; identical ending, and wanted them numbered in order. That is what $# is
; for: in a Replace value it becomes the number of this match, counting from
; one, so the first ending becomes 1, the second 2, and so on.
;
; Change the Find to whatever your passages actually end with.

[number each ending]
Find="\r?\n---END---"
Replace="\n[$#]"
